From f5a93d408f97a5c0de9835e571c92dd2649246a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Botcazou <ebotcazou@adacore.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:15:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Ada: Fix adjustment of function result on secondary stack in
 allocator

This is a regression present on the mainline and 16 branch, introduced by a
recent optimization: when function calls return on the secondary stack, the
result is effectively built as a temporary there and, therefore, needs to be
later copied to the allocated memory, which requires a call to Adjust if the
type is controlled.

gcc/ada/
	* exp_ch6.adb (Expand_Ctrl_Function_Call): Do not return early for
	the qualified expression of an allocator if the call returns on the
	secondary stack.
---
 gcc/ada/exp_ch6.adb | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/ada/exp_ch6.adb b/gcc/ada/exp_ch6.adb
index 950d03af386e..38d13e0e7cfd 100644
--- a/gcc/ada/exp_ch6.adb
+++ b/gcc/ada/exp_ch6.adb
@@ -5794,10 +5794,12 @@ package body Exp_Ch6 is
 
       --  The same optimization: if the returned value is used to initialize a
       --  dynamically allocated object, then no need to copy/readjust/finalize,
-      --  we can initialize it in place.
+      --  we can initialize it in place, provided that the call does not return
+      --  on the secondary stack.
 
       if Nkind (Par) = N_Qualified_Expression
         and then Nkind (Parent (Par)) = N_Allocator
+        and then not Use_Sec_Stack
       then
          return;
       end if;
